{
  "_comment": "Per-formula overrides for brew-changes' changelog resolution. `url` is a manual override for formulae whose real changelog isn't reachable through GitHub auto-detection: most aren't GitHub-native (GNU/GNOME/language runtimes/etc, pointed at their own site or a self-hosted git). `repo` (\"owner/repo\") names the GitHub repo for formulae that DO have one with real Releases (pnpm, gemini-cli, zed, redis, ruby, several casks) but whose Homebrew homepage/url fields don't reference GitHub, so auto-detection can't find it. `prerelease` shows only GitHub-flagged pre-releases, for preview channels (zed@preview) whose releases are interleaved with the stable channel's. `{version}`, `{major.minor}` and `{major}` in a URL are filled in from the version being upgraded to, for projects that publish notes per release, release branch or major series. HTML pages are converted to Markdown before matching version headings. Verified with `go run ./cmd/validate-changelogs 100` (and `-cask 100`) as of 2026-10-15; re-verify periodically since upstream projects reorganize docs. `lax_headings` opts a formula whose changelog file IS found via normal GitHub auto-detection into a looser version-heading match: some files (tmux's CHANGES, xz's NEWS) mark version sections with plain, unmarked lines rather than Markdown ATX/Setext headings, which the default strict matcher can't locate. Keys are normally a bare formula/cask name, but formulae from a third-party tap (e.g. dart-lang/dart/dart) must use their tap-qualified name here, since that's what `brew outdated`/homebrew.Package.Name report and what changelogconfig.Get is called with — Get does an exact match, no bare-name fallback.",
